--TEST--
`Core\Task::all`'s answer is a shape with the argument's own field names, each carrying that field's own declared return type rather than `mixed` — `rule:concurrency/all-answers-a-typed-shape`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 1 is written against exactly this: the uniform alternative answers
// `array<mixed>` and every call site then pays a cast, so what the member is
// *worth* is that `$page->rows` is an `array<int>` and `$page->label` a
// `string` with nothing written at the use site.
//
// A frozen diagnostic is how that is asserted without running anything: the
// scheduler half of § 1 is not on disk (`crates/nvs-stdlib/src/task.rs` owns
// what the body is until it is), so what a case can ask is what the *checker*
// believes. Each mis-declaration below quotes the field's own type back, and
// the two quote different types — which a collapsed `mixed` answer could not
// do, because it has only one type to quote for both.
class Page {
    public static function fields(): void {
        var $page = Core\Task::all({
            rows:  fn(): array<int> => [1, 2, 3],
            label: fn(): string     => "all",
        });
        string $rows = $page->rows;
        int $label = $page->label;
        echo $rows, $label;
    }
}

Page::fields();
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `array<int>`
   --> case.nvs:19:24
%A
error[E0401]: expected `int`, found `string`
   --> case.nvs:20:22
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
